{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "צרור את המדינים", :translit "tzror et ha-midyanim", :gloss "harass the Midianites"} {:he "לשון יחיד", :translit "lashon yachid", :gloss "singular form"} {:he "והכיתם", :translit "ve-hikitem", :gloss "and you shall smite them"} {:he "לשון רבים", :translit "lashon rabim", :gloss "plural form"} {:he "צרור", :translit "tzror", :gloss "harass"} {:he "כי על ידך היה", :translit "ki al yadecha hayah", :gloss "for through you it was"} {:he "אל תבעלי אלא לגדול שבהם", :translit "al tibba'eli ela le-gadol she-bahem", :gloss "do not lie with any but the greatest of them"} {:he "וזהו משה", :translit "ve-zehu moshe", :gloss "and this is Moses"} {:he "והכיתם לשון רבים ולא משה", :translit "ve-hikitem lashon rabim ve-lo moshe", :gloss "and smite them plural form and not Moses"} {:he "כי נתגדל במדין", :translit "ki nitgadel be-midyan", :gloss "for he had grown great in Midian"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Grammatical observation: צרור is singular address while והכיתם is plural; Moses is excluded from the smiting because he was raised in Midian."}], :frame {:text "Moses lived in Midian after fleeing Egypt, marrying Zipporah daughter of Jethro, and tending his flocks there (Exodus 2:15–21, Exodus 3:1). The narrative of Numbers 25 records that a Midianite woman, identified in Numbers 25:14 as Cozbi daughter of Zur, was brought to the camp. The tradition cited by Ba'al HaTurim that her father instructed her to seduce none other than Moses himself appears in Midrash Tanchuma, Pinchas 5. Moses's decades in Midian are the basis for the claim that he had grown great there.", :sources ["Exodus 2:15-21" "Exodus 3:1" "Numbers 25:14" "Midrash Tanchuma Pinchas 5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Grammatical observation: צרור is singular address while והכיתם is plural; Moses is excluded from the smiting because he was raised in Midian.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:36.860166561Z", :model "glm-5.2"}